    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n90589" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">προύνεικος</span></b>  or <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">προύνῑκος </span></b> ( <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">προυνικός</span></b> , <i><span class="en">
			Hsch.
		</span></i>), ὁ, (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἤνεικα</span>) <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>one who bears
				burdens out of</i> the market, <i>hired porter,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Com.Adesp.
				333
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				1343
			</span></i>, Hdn.Gr.<i><span class="en">
				2.445
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Ael.Dion.
				<u>Fr.</u>
				284
			</span></i> (as pr. n., <i><span class="en">
				<u>IG</u>
				3.1100.12
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				12
			</span></i> (<i><span class="en">
				8
			</span></i>).<i><span class="en">
				484
			</span></i>): Byz., acc. to <i><span class="en">
				Poll.
				7.132
			</span></i>; used as a term of abuse, <i>low fellow</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Herod.
				3.12
			</span></i>,<i><span class="en">
				65
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				D.L.
				4.6
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀνδράσι π.</span> prob. in Epic.
			ap. <i><span class="en">
				Ath.
				14.639d
			</span></i>: as Adj., <i>lewd</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">φιλήματα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>AP</u>
					12.209
				</span></i>
			 (<i><span class="en">
				Strat.
			</span></i>). (Derived fr. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πρό,
			ἐνείκω</span> by <i><span class="en">
				Ael.
			</span></i> Dion. l.c., cf. <i><span class="en">
				<u>AB</u>
				1415
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Phot.
			</span></i>; also expld. by 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πρό, νεῖκος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>EM</u>
					691.19
				</span></i>
			.)</div>
